description:
Readers can turn on sound for the already-playing hero story (apricitus-4e056d), and hear each step as it happens:
- the recording while it's analyzed (the sweep lasts as long as the audio);
- the slice once it's selected;
- each chop as it's cut;
- each chop landing in the composition, warped and tuned (taken from the real engine's render of its track);
- the drum groove, then the whole piece.

**Done when:** one click turns it on from anywhere in the story, and the audio clock drives the pictures. Turning it off returns to silent motion; chapter jumps re-sync; the sound holds when the hero is off-screen. Tests and a browser check pass.

comments.text:
Built and verified.

- **Assets:** scripts/hero-data.py now also writes web/public/hero/*.mp3 (608 KB): the two source windows (mono, level-matched), plus tracks b and h, each rendered alone by the engine. Each render gets a gain back to its level in the full mix, computed from the master make-up (both −1.6/−1.5 dB).
- **Story:**
  - the listen sweeps are linear and last as long as their windows;
  - the horns' phases moved later to fit;
  - the playhead runs in two sessions (29.5–34.5 s drums only; 58.5 s → end, both tracks);
  - glows pulse on whatever is sounding.
- **Engine:** web/src/ui/flow/sound.ts schedules on its own 100 ms timer with 1.2 s of lookahead. The first version scheduled from animation frames and dropped cues when frames were throttled.
- **Checks:**
  - logged every buffer start with a patched AudioBufferSourceNode.start: slice, 8 chops, drum landings, drum loop, horn landings, and both loops at 58.5 s, all at the right audio times and offsets;
  - sound off stops everything;
  - tests pass 4/4 (added a cue test); build OK.
